.TH NIBWARDEN 1 2026-11-06 "nibwarden" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nibwarden \- command-line client for the nibwarden vault daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nibwarden
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nibwarden
talks to
.BR nibwardend (1),
which keeps a Bitwarden or Vaultwarden vault unlocked for the desktop session.
The daemon is started on demand through the systemd user unit
.BR nibwardend.service .
.PP
Commands that read secrets need the vault unlocked.
When it is locked, the daemon shows its unlock window, or where no window can be shown,
.B nibwarden
asks for the master password on the terminal.
Programs other than nibwarden's own windows may have to be approved in a window first
(see
.B [approval]
in
.BR FILES ).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Account
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show the account and whether the vault is locked.
.TP
.B login \-\-email \fIaddress\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR \fIserver\fR] [\fB\-\-method authenticator\fR|\fBemail\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR]
Log in.
.I server
is
.BR bitwarden.com " (the default), " bitwarden.eu ,
or the https URL of a self-hosted server.
Two-step login asks for the code on the terminal.
.TP
.B logout
Log out, and delete the local session and the encrypted vault cache.
.TP
.B unlock \fR[\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR | \fB\-\-gui\fR | \fB\-\-terminal\fR]
Unlock with the master password: in the unlock window when one can be shown (a desktop
session, not over SSH), otherwise on the terminal.
\fB\-\-gui\fR and \fB\-\-terminal\fR choose one; \fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR reads it from stdin.
.TP
.B lock
Lock now.
.TP
.B sync \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR]
Sync with the server.
The daemon also syncs every five minutes and as soon as the server reports a change.
.SS Reading the vault
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIsearch\fR] [\fB\-\-folder\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
List items: names, kinds, folders and URIs, never secrets.
.TP
.B get \fIitem\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-field\fR \fIfield\fR] [\fB\-\-folder\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-no\-newline\fR]
Print one field of an item (by name or id).
.I field
is
.BR password " (the default), " username ", " totp ", " notes ", " uri ,
a card or SSH key field, or the name of a custom field.
.TP
.B read \fIreference\fR [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-no\-newline\fR]
Print the value of a reference
.BR nw:// [\fIfolder\fB/\fR]\fIitem\fB/\fIfield .
.TP
.B totp \fIitem\fR [\fB\-\-folder\fR \fIname\fR]
Print the item's current one-time code.
.TP
.B run \fR[\fB\-\-env\-file\fR \fIfile\fR]... \fB\-\-\fR \fIcommand\fR...
Run
.I command
with every
.B nw://
reference in its environment replaced by the value.
.I file
holds
.IB KEY = VALUE
lines added to the environment; later files win.
.TP
.B generate \fR[\fIoptions\fR]
Print a new password: \fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-length\fR \fIn\fR (20), \fB\-\-special\fR,
\fB\-\-no\-uppercase\fR, \fB\-\-no\-lowercase\fR, \fB\-\-no\-numbers\fR,
\fB\-\-avoid\-ambiguous\fR.
With \fB\-\-passphrase\fR, a passphrase: \fB\-\-words\fR \fIn\fR (5),
\fB\-\-separator\fR \fIs\fR (\-), \fB\-\-capitalize\fR, \fB\-\-include\-number\fR.
.SS SSH and git
.TP
.B ssh list \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
List the SSH keys the agent offers.
.TP
.B ssh authorize \fR[\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR]
Allow SSH signatures from this terminal session with the master password,
for when no approval window can be shown (for example over SSH).
Lasts until the vault locks.
.TP
.B ssh agent\-setup \fR[\fB\-\-remove\fR]
Make
.BR ssh (1)
use nibwarden's agent: adds a
.B Host *
block with
.B IdentityAgent
to
.IR ~/.ssh/config ,
before the first agent set there for every host, so it takes their place while hosts
set up with an agent of their own above it keep theirs.
ssh is asked
.RB ( "ssh \-G" )
whether the block takes effect; if not, the file is left as it was and the reason shown.
Running it again repairs a block that later edits put out of effect.
\fB\-\-remove\fR takes the block out again.
The settings window does the same.
.TP
.B ssh git\-setup \fR[\fB\-\-key\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-global\fR] | \fB\-\-remove\fR
Make git sign commits with an SSH key from the vault, through
.BR nibwarden\-ssh\-sign (1).
With \fB\-\-global\fR, a setup that another file git reads would override (an
.B [include]
after it) is refused and the git config left as it was.
\fB\-\-remove\fR stops that in the global git config (the allowed signers stay, so
earlier commits still verify).
The settings window does the same for the global git config.
.SS Browser extension
.TP
.B browser enable \fR[\fB\-\-replace\fR]
Register
.BR nibwarden\-browser\-host (1)
with the installed browsers (Firefox, Chrome, Chromium, Edge, Vivaldi, Brave), so the
official Bitwarden extension's "Unlock with biometrics" asks in nibwarden's window
instead of Bitwarden's desktop app.
A browser where Bitwarden's desktop app is registered is left alone unless
\fB\-\-replace\fR.
.TP
.B browser disable
Remove nibwarden's registration.
.TP
.B browser status
Show what each installed browser starts for the extension.
.SS Bitwarden Send
.TP
.B send list \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
List your Sends, never their content or link.
.TP
.B send create \fIname\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
Create a Send of the text on stdin, or of \fB\-\-file\fR \fIpath\fR (at most 10 MiB),
and print its link.
Options: \fB\-\-days\fR \fIn\fR (1 to 31, default 7), \fB\-\-max\-access\fR \fIn\fR,
\fB\-\-password\fR (asked on the terminal), \fB\-\-hidden\fR, \fB\-\-hide\-email\fR,
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fItext\fR.
.TP
.B send get \fIsend\fR [\fB\-\-text\fR]
Print a Send's link, or its text.
.TP
.B send delete \fIsend\fR
Delete a Send; its link stops working.
.SS Export and import
.TP
.B export \-o\fR|\fB\-\-output \fIfile\fR [\fB\-\-format encrypted\-json\fR|\fBjson\fR|\fBcsv\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR]
Export your personal items and folders in a format Bitwarden imports.
Always asks for the master password again; \fBencrypted\-json\fR (the default) also asks
for a password for the file.
\fBjson\fR and \fBcsv\fR are not encrypted, and CSV holds only logins and secure notes.
The file is created readable only by you; an existing file is replaced only with \fB\-\-force\fR.
.TP
.B import \fIfile\fR [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR]
Add the items of a Bitwarden JSON or CSV export (also password-protected)
or of a KeePass database (.kdbx) to the vault.
The format is detected; the file's password is asked for when it has one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
The daemon's control socket.
.TP
.B \-\-password\-stdin
Read passwords from lines of stdin instead of the terminal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NIBWARDEN_SOCKET
Same as \fB\-\-socket\fR.
Default:
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nibwarden/daemon.sock .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nibwarden/config.toml
Settings, also changed in the settings window.
Every key is optional:
.RS
.PP
.nf
[appearance]
theme = "system"          # "system", "light" or "dark"
language = "system"       # or a tag such as "zh-TW", "zh-CN", "en"
website_icons = true      # show websites' icons (the icon service sees the domains)

[lock]
idle_minutes = 15         # lock after this long unused; 0 = never
idle_action = "lock"      # then "lock", or "logout" (deletes the local copy too)
on_screen_lock = true
on_sleep = true

[approval]                # SSH signatures are always confirmed
remember = "application"  # "request", "application" or "terminal"
remember_hours = 0        # how long an approval lasts; 0 = until locked
read_secret = "ask"       # secrets read by programs: "ask" or "allow"
without_window = "allow"  # when no window can be shown (SSH)

[clipboard]
clear = true
clear_after_seconds = 90
minimize_after_copy = false

[unlock]
system = false            # unlock with the system's authentication (polkit) once
                          # the master password unlocked since nibwardend started

[tray]
enabled = false           # system tray icon, started at login
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 3 when the vault is locked (and could not be unlocked), 4 when not logged in;
2 on a usage error; 1 on any other error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nibwarden login \-\-email me@example.com
nibwarden get GitHub \-f totp
DB_PASSWORD=nw://Work/Database/password nibwarden run \-\- ./server
nibwarden export \-o vault.json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nibwardend (1),
.BR nibwarden\-gui (1),
.BR nibwarden\-ssh\-sign (1),
.BR nibwarden\-browser\-host (1)
